## Resolved mutable: m-cluster-draw-wrong-buffer-bound

PARTIAL. browser-135: a.renderer.attributes is undefined (three's WebGLAttributes is not on the public renderer API), so I cannot grab the geometry's GPU index buffer handle to bind it explicitly from the consumer/page. The bounds-guard I shipped (against index.array.length, browser-134) is SOUND -- drawn stays 429/429 (no over-cull) and maxDrawEndOverCpuBytes=0 -- but gl.getError stays 1282 because the BOUND GPU buffer is smaller than index.array (three has not uploaded the full combined index, or a different buffer is bound at _draw time). The real fix needs the lib to ensure ITS geometry's index buffer is bound before multiDraw (the lib has renderer access internally via onBeforeRender's renderer arg -> renderer.attributes IS available INSIDE the lib/three module scope, just not via the app's window.__app.renderer proxy). So the fix belongs INSIDE ../streaming-gltf _draw using the renderer passed to _render, not a page-level bind.